                        "entry_id": "605ef991-1282-31ac-a505-5ac2163d688e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A graveyard."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "97a4cd86-a49d-3044-bfc0-146f04cb73d0",
                        "entry_id": "605ef991-1282-31ac-a505-5ac2163d688e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In the game of dominoes, the pile of upside-down pieces that have yet to be used."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7735fa12-4e60-3373-951a-12d10bfcbca2",
                        "entry_id": "605ef991-1282-31ac-a505-5ac2163d688e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A dumpsite for obsolete or unusable aircraft etc; a junkyard."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1711a16b-dc7c-4441-96ff-3ecfee2595ce",
                                "sense_id": "7735fa12-4e60-3373-951a-12d10bfcbca2",
                                "text": "The “Boneyard” is a place of antiques and historic symbolism, a burial ground for aircraft."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e4ccffa-8618-4c54-91f9-df07820f3e2c",
                                "sense_id": "7735fa12-4e60-3373-951a-12d10bfcbca2",
                                "text": "Beginning in December 1969, the entire fleet was retired to the “boneyard” at Davis-Monthan AFB in Tucson, Arizona."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f332fda-1e12-4cfd-b92e-04d353e03390",
                                "sense_id": "7735fa12-4e60-3373-951a-12d10bfcbca2",
                                "text": "B-52s in a boneyard"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7df896c3-a6fe-4106-ba18-973bced124ef",
                                "sense_id": "7735fa12-4e60-3373-951a-12d10bfcbca2",
                                "text": "a 440 V-8 from the boneyard"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ea855d4-e606-42c3-bcef-87366d2b2bc6",
                                "sense_id": "7735fa12-4e60-3373-951a-12d10bfcbca2",
                                "text": "Or what is conveyed to those unversed in railway matters by reports following a shed visit that \"the frame of Claud Hamilton lay in the boneyard and had many endearing messages of farewell chalked on it\"?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ab693417-be6a-36ac-ac43-9f858b0c83f8",
                        "entry_id": "605ef991-1282-31ac-a505-5ac2163d688e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An area scraped down to the mineral soil, so that smouldering material can be placed there without starting another fire."
                        ],
